   "shape_h": "ol",
   "shape_m": "ol",
   "html_text": "The theory’s claims are genuine statements capable of truth or falsity. Any literal construal of a theory cannot change the logical relationships among the entities claimed by the theory—“most specifically, if a theory says that something exists, then a literal construal may elaborate on what that something is, but will not remove the implication of existence” (1980, 11).",
